# WHAT VERCEL DOES NOT NEED IN ORDER TO BUILD THIS SITE.
#
# There was no .vercelignore until 2026-09-15, so every deploy carried the
# whole repository into the build container — the test suite, the engineering
# docs, the QA registers and the design archive — none of which any build step
# opens. `npm run build` runs vite over src/ and index.html; `scripts/
# prerender.mjs` reads src/data and writes into dist/. Nothing below is touched
# by either.
#
# THIS DOES NOT AFFECT WHAT IS SERVED. Only files Vite emits into dist/ are
# published, so excluding these changes nothing a visitor can reach; it changes
# how much is uploaded and unpacked before the build starts.
#
# It is also NOT a security boundary. These files are public in the GitHub
# repository regardless — this is about deploy weight, not secrecy.

# The test suite. 94 MB on disk, and its report/ artifacts regenerate per run.
tests/

# Engineering documentation, proposals and QA registers — written for us.
docs/

# The design archive. Also gitignored; listed here so a local `vercel deploy`
# from the working directory does not sweep it up.
screenshots/
brand/

# Agent and editor state.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Anything a previous run left behind.
tmp/
.cache/
*.tmp.*
